/*Visual suggestion: Dashboard screenshot showing personalization performance metrics - conversion rate lift, revenue impact, engagement metrics. Include before/after comparison charts, segmentation breakdown, and key performance indicators. Design should look like a realistic analytics dashboard with data visualizations.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Illustration showing common personalization pitfalls - privacy violations, creepy targeting, data quality issues, organizational silos. Use cautionary colors (yellows, oranges, reds) and warning symbols. Style should be informative but not alarmist.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Roadmap infographic showing the three phases of personalization implementation from data foundation through rule-based personalization to AI-powered personalization. Include timelines, key milestones, and expected outcomes for each phase. Use a horizontal timeline format with distinct visual sections.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Visual representation of the 80/20 rule showing a bar chart or pie chart illustrating how 20% of personalization tactics drive 80% of results. Highlight the high-impact tactics (triggered emails, source-based personalization) versus lower-impact advanced tactics. Use contrasting colors to show the proportion clearly.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Three-panel illustration showing the analogies: 1) A skilled salesperson helping multiple customers simultaneously (representing scale), 2) Someone removing a blindfold to see clearly (representing data enabling understanding), 3) GPS dynamically recalculating routes (representing adaptive journeys). Clean, conceptual illustration style.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Checklist-style infographic showing the five key actions with icons, brief descriptions, and checkboxes. Use a vertical layout with each action clearly separated. Include estimated timelines or difficulty levels for each action. Professional, actionable design.*/
/*Visual suggestion: Concluding image showing the future vision of personalization - a seamless, respectful, valuable customer journey across multiple channels with the customer in control. Split-screen showing traditional generic marketing (cluttered, irrelevant, annoying) versus personalized future (clean, relevant, helpful). Optimistic but realistic tone.*/
